==Rules==
{{StageRule|13thAnni}}

==Battleground==
*1 [[Archbaron Face]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*15 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Countess Koryessa]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Effectively a hyperbuffed version of [[Fascinating Fallen Tower/Floor 16|Floor 16]], this is the first stage where money may become an actual concern if you haven't been collecting enough 経費. Kill Trolly Blogger and stall Archbaron Face with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]] until Countess Koryessa makes her appearance. Then start using Malizabeth as a platform to stack [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Rangers]] (only whenever Malizabeth is on the field), [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Rangers]] and [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Rangers]] alongside other tanky/Wave Immune attackers you might own ([[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] work too). Be conservative with your spending, since anything you send out will likely be killed by Archbaron Face as soon as Countess Koryessa gets knocked back. Luckily, by the time Countess Koryessa dies, there won't be anything in your way anymore, and Baron Face will be a lamb to the slaughter. Use things like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], or just plain [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Rangers]]/[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cats]] to take care of his remaining HP.

